# Product principles (always on)

Full source: `docs/PRODUCT_PRINCIPLES.md`. Follow it for every change.

## Non-negotiables

- Primary user is a preschooler (4–7). **Do not require reading for chrome/instructions.**
- Action controls may keep a short German word but **must include a clear vector/ASCII icon** (no emoji in buttons). Continue trailing-aligned.
- Practice chrome: back/forward chevrons above progress bar; speaker in the task area above the title; safe-area insets + extra bottom padding.
- Success: speak answer → star in upper third → wait for audio before next task. No speak-only “Sag…” screens with only Continue.
- No decorative pack titles or “Sprich mit!”-style instruction headlines in the practice shell.
- Fibel order: letters (upper+lower as two frames) → syllables → compose words from syllables → whole words → sentences.
- Letter TTS: “Finde den Buchstaben {a}.” — not “Aa”. Puzzle tiles without emoji icons; muted “ABC” watermark only.
- No fake wrong-answer distractors; freeware, ad-free, offline-capable core.
- Exercise layout: prompt upper-center, answers bottom-center (`ExerciseStage`).
- Math: exactly 3 choices; miss feedback spoken only; prefer tasks including quantity 1 (singular/plural language).

## When principles conflict with older plan text

Prefer `docs/PRODUCT_PRINCIPLES.md` and explicit user decisions in the current session. Document the drift; do not silently ignore the principles.
